---
title: "calc_interest (Pebble Protocol: Interest Model)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_mid: util_rate <= mid_kink?
    q_check_mid --> q_low_segment: yes (low utilization)
    q_check_mid --> q_check_high: no
    q_low_segment --> q_low_calc: weight = util_rate / mid_kink
    q_low_calc --> q_low_range: range = borrow_rate_on_mid_kink - base_rate
    q_low_range --> q_low_result: rate = weight * range + base_rate
    q_low_result --> [*]: return borrow_rate
    q_check_high --> q_high_check: util_rate <= high_kink?
    q_high_check --> q_mid_segment: yes (mid utilization)
    q_high_check --> q_high_segment: no (high utilization)
    q_mid_segment --> q_mid_calc: weight = (util_rate - mid_kink) / (high_kink - mid_kink)
    q_mid_calc --> q_mid_range: range = borrow_rate_on_high_kink - borrow_rate_on_mid_kink
    q_mid_range --> q_mid_result: rate = weight * range + borrow_rate_on_mid_kink
    q_mid_result --> [*]: return borrow_rate
    q_high_segment --> q_high_calc: weight = (util_rate - high_kink) / (1 - high_kink)
    q_high_calc --> q_high_range: range = max_borrow_rate - borrow_rate_on_high_kink
    q_high_range --> q_high_result: rate = weight * range + borrow_rate_on_high_kink
    q_high_result --> [*]: return borrow_rate

    note right of q_low_segment
        INV-001: interest rate is continuous and piecewise linear
        INV-002: at util_rate = 0, rate = base_rate
        INV-003: at util_rate = mid_kink, rate = borrow_rate_on_mid_kink
        INV-004: at util_rate = high_kink, rate = borrow_rate_on_high_kink
        INV-005: at util_rate = 1.0, rate = max_borrow_rate
    end note
